S OUT BY LINE NUMBER, AND THEN TYPE IN THE STARTING LINE NUMBER TO DUMP THE SCREEN AREA INTO.   TO RETURN TO THE MAIN MENU, TYPE "A".     STARTING OVER FROM SCRATCH   YOU CAN ERASE THE ENTIRE CONTENTS OF THE SCREEN AREA, AND START OVER.  TO DO THIS,CHANGE THE DEVICE VIA A NUMBER INSTALLED ON THE BOOT DISK.  YOU CAN DO THIS BY HITTING "C".  THEN TELL IT WHICH DEVICE NUMBER TO USE, AND FOLLOW ITS INSTRUCTIONS.  THERE IS ALSO A BUILT-IN SEQUENTIAL FILE READER, WHICH YOU CAN USE TO VIEW DOC FILES, GRAPALL ITS NEATO FEATURES (SOME THAT DON'T SHOW UP IN *ANY* OTHER PROGRAMS!)   AFTER YOU HAVE FOLLOWED ALL THE PROPER PROMPTS TO GET INTO EDIT MODE, YOU WILL SEE EITHER THE PICTURE THAT YOU PULLED FROM THE BUFFER (IF IN FACT YOU DID PULL ONE OUT) OR YOU WIF2:  TURN TRAIL MODE ON/OFF (EXPLAINED LATER)F3:  UNDO-  HIT *TWICE* TO ERASE ALL EDITING DONE SINCE THE LAST TIME YOU HIT 'F1' FROM EDIT MODE.  HAVING TO HIT THE KEY TWICE IS A SAFEGUARD AGAINST THOSE WITHOUT NIMBLE FINGERS.(NO OFFENSE INTENDED-OF COMAIN MENU.  THIS WILL LEAVE THE SCREEN AREA BUFFER INTACT**ONLY IF PREVIOUSLY STORED WITH 'S' STORE COMMAND!**F7:  QUICK HELP SCREEN.  ALLOWS USER TO QUICKLY REMIND HIM/HERSELF OF WHAT FUNCTION KEYS DO WHAT.F8:  TURN RAINBOW MODE ON/OFF-  WHEN YOU TANIPULATE THE GRAPHICS YOU CREATE.   HERE ARE THE OPTIONS AVAILABLE FROM THE EDIT MENU, AND A BRIEF SUMMARY OF EACH:"E":  GO BACK TO EDIT MODE.  CONTINUE MANUAL WORK ON SUBJECT."C":  COPY IMAGE.  USE CURSOR AND RETURN KEYS TO DESIGNATE AREA TO COPY.KALEIDOSCOPE "UNDO"S ALL THE STAMPING."M":  MOVE MODE.  USE THE SAME AS COPY MODE, EXCEPT IT ERASES THE ORIGINAL."*":  MERGE MODE.  ALLOWS COPYING FROM A FILE ON DISK OR TAPE.  TYPE IN THE FILENAME, THEN HOLD SPACEBAR TO SCROLL TO WHAT YOU WANT TO ME MODE.  ONE OF KALEIDOSCOPE'S MORE ADVANCED FEATURES.  ALLOWS YOU TO MAKE A "REFLECTION" OF THE IMAGE.  USE IT THE SAME WAY AS YOU  WOULD USE THE COPY, EXCEPT YOU HAVE THE OPTION TO FLIP IT HORIZONTALLY OR VERTICALLY."I":  INVERT IMAGE.  MUCH LIKE THE E IT."R":  REVERSE AN AREA.  THIS FUNCTION ALLOWS YOU TO LITERALLY REVERSE AN IMAGE.  USE CURSOR AND RETURN KEYS TO DESIGNATE AREA, AND ALL CHARACTERS IN THAT AREA WILL BECOME REVERSED."CTRL-C":  COLOR CHANGE/SEEK.  CHOOSE "S" TO SEEK A COLOR AND CHAN␀ USE THE COLOR "P" PICK OPTION, HIT "P" AT THE COLOR PROMPTS, AND MOVE THE CURSOR TO THE SPOT ON THE SCREEN (OR THE COLOR BAR AT THE BOTTOM).  WHEN THE BORDER COLOR CHANGES TO THE COLOR YOU WANT TO CHANGE TO (OR FROM), HIT RETURN."B":  BACKGROUND.  THI HIT "R" TO "REDO" THE SCREEN.  THEN FOLLOW SAME INSTRUCTIONS FOR THE "EDIT" COMMAND.  TO ABORT WITH SCREEN AREA INTACT, HIT "A".      VIEWING A DISK DIRECTORY   AT ANY OF THE 3 MENUS--DOS, EDIT MENU, AND MAIN MENU, YOU CAN VIEW A DIRECTORY BY SIMPLYCAN VIEW A DIRECTORY, TOO (SEE ABOVE).  FROM HERE YOU CAN ALSO CHANGE THE DEVICE THAT THE PROGRAM IS ACCESSING AS A DISK DRIVE (8-11).  TO DO THIS, HIT "#" AND TELL THE COMPUTER WHAT DEVICE YOU WANT.   ONE MORE HANDY THING THAT KALEIDOSCOPE CAN DO IS TO HICS, OR FONTS (CBM GRAPHIC FONTS) WITH.  USE THIS BY HITTING THE "/" KEY.   TO ABORT FROM THE DOS MENU, HIT RETURN.      GETTING DOWN TO BUSINESS.   ONCE YOU ARE IN EDIT MODE, THAT IS WHERE ALL THE FUN STARTS.  HERE IS WHERE KALEIDOSCOPE SHOWS OFF LL SEE A BLANK SCREEN WITH THE CURSOR AT THE HOME POSITION AND THE STATUS BAR SAYING CHEERFULLY "EDIT MODE".   FROM THIS POINT, YOU HAVE 8 DIRECT-ACCESS FUNCTION KEYS:F1:  "SNAPSHOT" THE IMAGE AND GO TO EDIT MENU (EXPLAINED FURTHER ON IN THIS FILE).URSE)F4:  SET/ERASE TAB-  CHECK INDICATOR AT BOTTOM OF SCREEN FOR AN ARROW ON THAT COLUMN INDICATING A TAB STOP.F5:  TAB TO NEXT COLUMN TO THE RIGHT WITH TAB STOP.  IF THERE IS NO TAB STOPS, IT STOPS AUTOMATICALLY AT RIGHTMOST COLUMN.F6:  ABORT TO URN RAINBOW ON, EVERYTHING YOU TYPE COMES OUT IN MULTIPLE CYCLING COLORS.  WORKS WITH BACKGROUND, TRAIL, AND BORDER MODES.  ALSO SEE "^R" COMMAND IN "EDIT MENU" SECTION.            EDIT MENU   FROM HERE, YOU CAN ACCESS THE MANY AWESOME OPTIONS THAT M  THEN USE CURSOR KEYS TO MOVE IMAGE AROUND ON SCREEN, AND USE RETURN KEY TO STAMP.  CONTINUE STAMPING AS MUCH AS YOU LIKE.  SPACEBAR SWITCHES UNDERLAY/OVERLAY/COPY MODE (ONLY KALEIDOSCOPE HAS IT!) AND F1 STORES PICTURE.  IF YOU MESS UP, JUST HIT F3 AND RGE.  HIT "F1" TO START COPYING, AND USE THE SAME AS COPY MODE.  THERE ARE MANY FILES INCLUDED IN THIS KALEIDOSCOPE PACKAGE, INCLUDING A BUNCH OF NEAT FONTS AND SOME GREAT CLIP ART BY SOME OF THE BEST ARTISTS HERE IN PDX (NAMELY ME & KEN!)"<-":  MIRRORMIRROR IMAGE FUNCTION, EXCEPT THAT THE IMAGE NEED NOT BE MOVED.  THIS IS USEFUL FOR CASES IN WHICH YOU SIMPLY WANT TO FLIP AN IMAGE, WITHOUT COPYING IT."CTRL-E":  ERASE AREA.  USE THE CURSOR AND RETURN KEYS TO DESIGNATE AREA, AND KALEIDOSCOPE WILL ERAS	GE IT TO ANOTHER, OR TYPE "C" TO CHANGE ALL COLORS IN AN AREA TO ONE DESIGNATED COLOR.  USE CURSOR AND RETURN KEYS TO DESIGNATE AN AREA AND KALEIDOSCOPE WILL CHANGE THE COLORS.  THEN USE F1 TO RE-PICK A COLOR OR JUST HIT "Y" IF IT'S OK THE WAY IT IS.  TO HITTING THE "$" KEY.      USING THE BUILT-IN DOS SHELL   FROM EITHER THE MAIN MENU OR THE EDIT MENU, YOU CAN ACCESS THE BUILT-IN DOS MENU BY HITTING THE "@" KEY.  AT THIS POINT, YOU HAVE THE ABILITY TO SEND A DISK COMMAND BY HITTING "@" AGAIN.  YOU 
